A||||11||Oreif||Subwoofer Q's or idea's.||||1||
Z||000000||Oreif||11-06-2000||12:16 PM||||I'm looking to install an 8" sub in my car.<BR>I was looking at the console mounted version but RSM no longer sells the console. I would prefer not placing in behind the seat since I need the drivers seat all the way back and all the amps, surround sound processor and crossover will be behind the passenger seat. Has anyone built a box for an 8" sub that goes in the area of the factory sub? I have seen the footwell subs and prefer not to put it there. (wife is tall too) I want to keep it in the interior of the car. If anyone has the RSM console in gray and wants to get rid of it let me know. The sub box only needs to be .3 cu.ft. minimum. Any other idea's or pics would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Thanks,<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||11-06-2000||12:48 PM||||Your wife must be NBA material...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Seriously, I'm 6'6" and have no problem sitting on the passenger side with my footwell stufed with a 10" sub.  My enclosure is actually a bit oversized. I'm sure with an 8" sub you could probably have an extra 2-3" of foot room. But you are kinda ruling out the majority of the feasible options, you might want to cosider Bass Shakers under the seats.  They wont give you the hump of a big woofer witha powerful amp, but it will give you some feel of low end power to your tunes.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-06-2000||01:07 PM||||Stimpy, Do you have pics of the footwell sub? What is the cu.ft. of the 10" box. The reason I'm worried about foot space it the passenger seat will be moved forward to accommidate the electronics. I could possibly get away with 1 "click" forward on the seat. I thought someone did the 8" in the stock sub area but I could not find the thread. I may still consider the footwell sub. Do you have dimensions of the box? I have heard "Bass Shakers" and and prefer a regular woofer.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||11-06-2000||01:34 PM||||Oreif,<P>You are correct.  There has been discussion of a down-firing 8" sub mounted vertically under the dash.  I even remember seeing a web page on the subject.  A mechanic in Australia or S. Africa did a great write up on the subject.  <P>If my failing memory serves me, the instructions were fairly simple.  He actually chose to manufacture the enclosure out of PVC pipe.  I have done some preliminary searching for components of this type of install to no avail.  I am going to be working on a cubic enclosure for the same location in the near future.  <P>Currently I am running a 10" in the passenger footwell of my Fiero.  Just ask fiero56 how comfortable it is to ride over there (it's not!).  Not to mention that the sub is in plain view for untrustworthy types... and yes one such idiot tried to break into my car using only my radio antennae!  The important thing is that he was far too stupid to accomplish his/her goal.  <P>Later,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||11-06-2000||02:41 PM||||WTIII, I FOUND IT! I thought it was a thread on here but it's a website. Thanks! The link to the 8" sub under the dash is: <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~qmekanic/subwoof.html" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~qmekanic/subwoof.html</A> <P>I'm not sure about using an 8" PVC pipe but I am going to take measurements tomorrow and see if I can make a box to fit. I am going to try for a sealed box first. According to the link above I have about 4-5 inches of depth. If I move the "blue dingy thingy" I think I could get a box around .4 cu.ft. in there. (The woofer I have requires .3 to .5).<BR>I'll keep everyone informed as to how it goes. Also I will make sure I make detailed drawings of the enclosure so it can be copied in case others like the idea.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
